            "review_text": "familyof4Singapore\nsingapore9 contributions\n0\nHorrible Experience and Very Expensive Food in Chinatown\nMay 2018 • Friends\nWas there for late lunch after shopping trip in Chinatown. Restaurant helper could speak cantonese, so ordering food was a breeze. Upon recommendations, ordered Stir Fry Noodle and Fried Rice - medium size serving and 4 fresh coconut for 4 ladies. Food was normal, but price was shocking. We were charged about $650,000.00 Dong for what we ordered. When we questioned the Cashier and asked for menu to check, she claimed menu does not indicate the price for the serving that we ordered. We found this restaurant is clearly a tourist trap. Pls avoid this at all cost.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten May 29, 2018",
